KG42.register("rules-86d6c6063dbd6d4253940b32",{"id":"36-dsm_mechanism_design::v141-c-R009","paper":"36-dsm_mechanism_design","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R009","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M03","name":"Market payment","process_stage":"settlement","market_meaning":"Each user's slot payment equals its own slot consumption multiplied by p_k evaluated at the aggregate consumption of all users in that slot. Scope: Each user's per-slot payment in the price-anticipating single-price game. Condition: Given the users' consumption profile.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function settlement.payment under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["settlement.payment"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Each user's per-slot payment in the price-anticipating single-price game.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E25"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R009-x-n-k","symbol":"x_n^k","meaning":"Power consumption level of user n in time slot k; the k-th component of the consumption vector x_n selected by user n in the price-anticipating game.","kind":"operational","domain":"x_n^k is the k-th component of a vector x_n ∈ X_n, where X_n is user n's feasible energy-consumption set; the exact per-slot bounds are not stated in the supplied E25 quotation.","unit":null,"indices":["n","k"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E25","v141-b-g01-E27"]}],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R009-p-k","symbol":"p_k","meaning":"Single-price schedule function for time slot k, evaluated at aggregate slot consumption; the provider sets μ_k(x)=p_k(∑_{n∈N} x_n^k).","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"p_k(\\cdot)"},"unit":null,"indices":["k"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E25","v141-b-g01-E26"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R009-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Each user's slot payment equals its own slot consumption multiplied by p_k evaluated at the aggregate consumption of all users in that slot. Scope: Each user's per-slot payment in the price-anticipating single-price game. Condition: Given the users' consumption profile.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E25"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R009-C002","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"For each user n and each time slot k, the user's payment for that slot is its own slot consumption x_n^k multiplied by the single price p_k evaluated at the sum of all users' slot consumptions.","expression":"\\mathrm{payment}_n^k = x_n^k \\, p_k\\!\\left(\\sum_{m\\in\\mathcal{N}} x_m^k\\right), \\quad n\\in\\mathcal{N}.","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R009-x-n-k"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R009-p-k"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E25","v141-b-g01-E26"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E25","location":{"location_id":"src-0fb1d9d41e-p05-c1r4__v141-a-M03-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":"1174","section":"II-D-2 Price Anticipating Users","anchor_text":"for resource allocation. Given , the energy A. provider sets a single price for time slot . User the","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"We consider the following pricing scheme for resource allocation. Given \\mathbf{x}=(\\mathbf{x}_1,\\ldots,\\mathbf{x}_N), the energy provider sets a single price \\mu_k(\\mathbf{x})=p_k(\\sum_{n\\in\\mathcal{N}} x_n^k) for time slot k. User n then pays x_n^k p_k(\\sum_{m\\in\\mathcal{N}} x_m^k) for that time slot."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E26","location":{"location_id":"src-0fb1d9d41e-p05-c1r4__v141-a-M03-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":"1174","section":"II-D-2 Price Anticipating Users","anchor_text":"for resource allocation. Given , the energy A. provider sets a single price for time slot . User the","equation_id":"(13)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"We use the notation \\mathbf{x}_{-n} to denote the vector of all consumption powers chosen by users other than user n, i.e., \\mathbf{x}_{-n}=(\\mathbf{x}_1,\\ldots,\\mathbf{x}_{n-1},\\mathbf{x}_{n+1},\\ldots,\\mathbf{x}_N). Then, given \\mathbf{x}_{-n}, the payoff of each user n is obtained as Q_n(\\mathbf{x}_n;\\mathbf{x}_{-n}) = U_n\\left(\\sum_{k\\in\\mathcal{K}} x_n^k\\right) - \\sum_{k\\in\\mathcal{K}} x_n^k p_k\\left(\\sum_{m\\in\\mathcal{N}} x_m^k\\right). \\tag{13} The payoff function Q_n is similar to P_n, defined for price-taking users in (11). The only difference is that while the payoff function P_n takes the price \\lambda_k as a fixed parameter, price anticipating users realize that the price is set according to p_k(\\sum_{m\\in\\mathcal{N}} x_m^k), and adjust their payoffs accordingly."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E27","location":{"location_id":"src-0fb1d9d41e-p05-c2r1__v141-a-M03-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":"1174","section":"II-D-2 Price Anticipating Users","anchor_text":"IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON SMART GRID, VOL. 3, NO. 3, SEPTEMBER 2012 off From (13), the payoff of each use","equation_id":"(14)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"From (13), the payoff of each user depends on its power consumption as well as the power consumptions of other users. Hence, we have the following game among the users: Players: Registered users in set \\mathcal{N}. Strategies: Each user n \\in \\mathcal{N} selects its energy consumption level \\mathbf{x}_n \\in \\mathcal{X}_n to maximize its payoff. Payoffs: Q_n(\\mathbf{x}_n;\\mathbf{x}_{-n}) for each user n \\in \\mathcal{N} as in (13). A Nash equilibrium of the game defined by (Q_1,\\ldots,Q_N) is a vector \\mathbf{x} such that for all n \\in \\mathcal{N}, Q_n(\\mathbf{x}_n;\\mathbf{x}_{-n}) \\ge Q_n(\\bar{\\mathbf{x}}_n;\\mathbf{x}_{-n}), \\quad \\bar{\\mathbf{x}}_n \\in \\mathcal{X}_n. \\tag{14}"}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M03-clearing","v141-a-M03-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"settlement.payment","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E25","quote":"Given \\mathbf{x}=(\\mathbf{x}_1,\\ldots,\\mathbf{x}_N), the energy provider sets a single price \\mu_k(\\mathbf{x})=p_k(\\sum_{n\\in\\mathcal{N}} x_n^k) for time slot k. User n then pays x_n^k p_k(\\sum_{m\\in\\mathcal{N}} x_m^k) for that time slot."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"e2c884c31d6e3d799474ae090fdf9df3f412e87262481f217769c2343cddde44","applicability":"formalized","reason":"The supplied quotation explicitly gives the per-slot payment as x_n^k p_k(∑_{m∈N} x_m^k) for user n in slot k. The frozen graph contains the settlement.payment node, so the formula is formalized as a property of that node. B evidence remains UNREVIEWED; no independent source audit is claimed. Units and the exact per-slot feasible domain of x_n^k are not stated in the supplied E25 quotation and are left unspecified/flagged.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R009-x-n-k","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"x_n^k is the user's own slot consumption that multiplies the price function in the settlement.payment formula."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R009-p-k","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"p_k is the single-price schedule function evaluated at aggregate slot consumption in the settlement.payment formula."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R009-C002","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The constraint is the defining equation for the settlement.payment relation, expressing each user's per-slot payment in terms of its slot consumption and the single price evaluated at aggregate slot consumption."}],"revision_requests":["Re-extract and verify the exact per-slot feasible domain for x_n^k from the source's definition of X_n (equations (1)-(2)); the supplied E25 quotation only states that x_n^k appears in the payment formula.","Re-extract and verify the units of x_n^k and p_k from the source; the supplied E25 quotation does not state units."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
